<section id="top">
        <div class="page-shell about-page-intro">
            <span class="eyebrow">No app to install</span>
            <h1>No-app site inspections for Canadian field teams.</h1>
            <p class="page-lede">Picture a crew arriving on a site outside Calgary at first light. The driver needs a vehicle pre-use check, the foreman needs a site safety walk, and the operator needs to log the condition of the lift before it runs. Today that is three paper forms on a clipboard, or three logins to a tablet app nobody wants to carry. With Quickler it is one WhatsApp chat on the phone each of them already has. They answer by text, voice note or photo, and every check lands as a structured digital record a manager can read in real time.</p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-tight">
        <div class="content-duo">
            <div class="section-frame">
                <div class="section-header">
                    <div>
                        <p class="section-label">A day on site</p>
                        <h2>Three checks, one chat, nothing to download.</h2>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="detail-body">
                    <p>The reason paper and tablet apps slow a field crew down is friction at the edges. Paper has to be carried, photographed and re-typed back at the office. Tablet apps need a device per worker, a login, an install and a software update before anyone can start. Quickler removes both by running the inspection inside the messaging app already on the phone.</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>The driver runs the vehicle walkround before pulling out, answering each item in the chat</li>
                        <li>The foreman runs the site safety walk on arrival, snapping photos of any hazard straight into the thread</li>
                        <li>The operator logs the equipment pre-use check, flagging a worn sling with a voice note</li>
                        <li>A new starter needs no setup; once they have your number they can complete their first check</li>
                        <li>No tablets to buy, charge, track or replace when one is dropped on a job</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p>The crew never leaves WhatsApp, and the office never waits for paper to come back from the field.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="section-frame">
                <div class="section-header">
                    <div>
                        <p class="section-label">What the manager sees</p>
                        <h2>A live record, not a stack of PDFs to chase.</h2>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="detail-body">
                    <p>Each completed check becomes a clean, structured digital record on a manager dashboard. It is machine-readable and searchable, so a supervisor can see every crew and every site without opening a single attachment.</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Red, amber and green status surfaces faults the moment a worker flags them</li>
                        <li>The worn sling or the cracked windscreen shows up against the asset, not buried in a photo roll</li>
                        <li>Records are searchable across drivers, vehicles, equipment and sites over time</li>
                        <li>When a client, insurer or auditor wants a document, you export a PDF from the record in one click</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p>The PDF is there when you need it, but it is the convenient export, not the system of record. The structured data underneath is what lets a manager spot a recurring fault before it becomes an incident.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

